{"name":"Pursuit of Happiness","hex":"#f1d260","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pursuit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of pursuing.","A hobby or recreational activity, done regularly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pursuit"},{"term":"happiness","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The emotion of being happy; joy; elation.","Prosperity, thriving, wellbeing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/happiness"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Pursuit of Happiness (1934 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Pursuit of Happiness is a 1934 American historical comedy film directed by Alexander Hall and written by Stephen Morehouse Avery, J.P. McEvoy and Virginia Van Upp. The film stars Francis Lederer, Joan Bennett, Charlie Ruggles, Mary Boland, Walter Kingsford, Minor Watson and Adrian Morris. The film was released on September 28, 1934, by Paramount Pictures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b8/The_Pursuit_of_Happiness_%281934_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pursuit_of_Happiness_(1934_film)","wikidata":"Q4006586"},{"title":"The Pursuit of Happiness (1971 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Pursuit of Happiness is a 1971 American drama film about a student who goes on the run to avoid serving his full prison sentence for vehicular manslaughter. The film was directed by Robert Mulligan. The producer was David Susskind and the associate producer Alan Shayne. The movie was based on the novel by Thomas Rogers, with a screenplay written by Jon Boothe and George L. Sherman."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3c/The_Pursuit_of_Happiness_VideoCover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pursuit_of_Happiness_(1971_film)","wikidata":"Q7758822"},{"title":"Pursuit of Happiness (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Pursuit of Happiness\" is a song by American musician Kid Cudi, respectively featuring production and vocals from American electronic rock duo Ratatat and American neo-psychedelic act MGMT. The song was officially released on September 15, 2009, as the third single from Cudi's debut album, Man on the Moon: The End of Day (2009)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a4/Pursuitofhappinesscover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pursuit_of_Happiness_(song)","wikidata":"Q583143"},{"title":"Pursuit of Happiness (Arthur Loves Plastic album)","blocks":[{"text":"Pursuit of Happiness is the thirteenth album from Arthur Loves Plastic and was released in 2006."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/86/Arthur_Loves_Plastic_-_Pursuit_of_Happiness_%28Reissue%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pursuit_of_Happiness_(Arthur_Loves_Plastic_album)","wikidata":"Q7261585"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e8/Arthur_Loves_Plastic_-_Pursuit_of_Happiness.jpg/250px-Arthur_Loves_Plastic_-_Pursuit_of_Happiness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e8/Arthur_Loves_Plastic_-_Pursuit_of_Happiness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e8/Arthur_Loves_Plastic_-_Pursuit_of_Happiness.jpg/250px-Arthur_Loves_Plastic_-_Pursuit_of_Happiness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArthur_Loves_Plastic_-_Pursuit_of_Happiness.jpg"}],"sounds":{"pursuit":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e8/En-uk-pursuit.ogg?utm_source=en.w